course: dictionary
lesson: 1210
title: Budgerigar or budgie?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have a long name and a short name. «Budgies, short for budgerigars, are small parrots from the dry grasslands of Australia.» The words short for tell you that budgie is a shorter way of saying budgerigar. Both words mean the same bird.
explain: The context gives you clues. The sentence says budgies are small parrots, so a budgerigar must be a small parrot too. It also says they come from Australia, so you now know where they live in the wild.
explain: Look at the picture the sentence paints: «they fly in huge flocks that look like a green cloud». A flock is a large group of birds flying together. You can work out what flock means from the words around it, just as you would for any new word.
fact: A budgerigar is a small, long-tailed parrot.
fact: Budgie is the short, informal name for a budgerigar, and it is the friendly everyday word.
fact: Wild budgerigars are usually green and yellow.
fact: Pet budgies come in many colours.
fact: Budgerigars come from the dry grasslands of Australia.
exercise: «Budgies, short for budgerigars, are small parrots.» What does short for mean here? | Shorter than a parrot | *A shorter name for the same thing | Cut into small pieces | A short, quick visit
exercise: Where do wild budgerigars come from? | Brazil | Canada | *Australia | The Arctic
exercise: «They fly in huge flocks that look like a green cloud.» What is a flock? | A single bird with a long tail | *A large group of birds flying together | A cage with mirrors and bells | A cloud that is green
test: Which word is the informal, friendly name for a budgerigar? | Grassland | Flock | *Budgie | Parrot
test: Pet budgies come in many colours, but wild budgies are usually which two colours? | Black and white | Pink and purple | Red and blue | *Green and yellow
exam: Read: «Budgies, short for budgerigars, are small parrots from the dry grasslands of Australia.» Why does the writer say short for budgerigars? | To show the bird is named after a short man | To show budgies are short birds with no tails | To show the budgie is smaller than all other birds | *To show that budgie is a shorter name for the same bird
